  "metadata": {
    "lastUpdated": "2026-08-10",
    "notes": "Device-first schema. One entry per physical breaker; circuits nest underneath. Shed lists live on devices via shedIn so common-trip behaviour is explicit and there is one source of truth. Not every device is a breaker: role 'feedThrough' is a bus tap with no overcurrent protection, and what it feeds lives in subpanels[]. Handwritten panel directory cards are historical, not authoritative.",
    "changelog": [
      {
        "version": "2.6",
        "date": "2026-08-10",
        "summary": "Two more findings closed by owner confirmation. A-mwbc-overlap resolved: slots 5/7, 10/12 and 13/15 in Panel A are genuinely multi-wire branch circuits - two 120V legs sharing a neutral under one common-trip handle, not 240V loads - so circuitType drops 'probable'. What survives from that finding is narrower and now lives in A-unmapped: A-5-7 and A-10-12 each have a second leg (slots 5 and 12) with no endpoints recorded. B-2-4-oven resolved: the double oven is confirmed at 14/16, and the directory card's second 'Oven' at 5/7 is simply wrong. Likely cause recorded on B-6-8 - slots 5/7 face the feed-through lug and the 2/0 feeder conductors probably make that pair unusable, which also means Panel B has fewer than 14 genuinely available slots for expansion."
      }
    ]
  },
